  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Marsabit Drought Emergency Response 2017 DEC supported</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a project that targets to reach people in Marsabit County who have been devastated by recent severe drought.  Prolonged drought in Kenya has resulted in water &amp; pasture shortages and food insecurity situation. The crisis was exacerbated by the failure of the October-December 2016 short rains. Hundreds of livestock have died from starvation and people have been affected by hunger-related ailments while rates of child malnutrition has reached alarming levels.  In February 2017, the Government of Kenya declared the drought a national disaster and appealed for international support to save the lives of vulnerable people threatened by drought.  
CAFOD through DEC support is planning to work with Caritas Marsabit to address issues of water shortage, food insecurity and retention of children in schools.  CAFOD and partners will work through existing humanitarian forums both at national &amp; the County levels to maximise available support. 
The Key outcomes are;
- Improved access to safe and clean water for 400HHs 
- Improved access to life-saving food though Unconditional Cash Transfers (650HHs) and food distribution (740HHs)
- Increased household income for 500HHs through Cash for work
- Increased regular attendance of schools by 128 Children in 8 secondary schools
- Strengthened CSG coordination at 2 sub-county levels.</narrative>
  </description>
